{{!-- TRAVEL MAP — one of the book's regional maps, as large as the reader wants it, with the whole
      route planner on it.

      This is the "See the whole map" window, and it is a PEER of the route step, not a picture of
      it: the same origin picker, the same map tabs, the same hotspots and the same readout, all
      from the same partials the walkthrough uses. Picking here writes to the same trip.

      Structurally it is ImageZoomWindow's template with chrome added above and below. That window
      already looks for its viewport as a descendant when the root is not the viewport itself
      (see its activateListeners), which is exactly the case this template creates — so all of the
      wheel/drag/fit behaviour comes along untouched.

      The chrome does NOT ride the picture: only `.stonetop-image-zoom-overlay` is sized onto the
      image, so the controls and the readout stay put while the map moves behind them. --}}
<div class="stonetop-travel-map stonetop-journey{{#if journey.needsStart}} is-needing-start{{/if}}">

  <div class="stonetop-travel-map-chrome">
    {{> "stonetop.expedition-journey-controls" journey=journey}}
  </div>

  {{#if journey.map}}
  <div class="stonetop-image-zoom-view">
    <img class="stonetop-image-zoom-img" src="{{src}}" alt="{{alt}}" draggable="false">
    <div class="stonetop-image-zoom-overlay stonetop-journey-canvas">{{{overlay}}}</div>
  </div>
  {{else}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-nomap">
    That map isn&rsquo;t in this world. Run <strong>Import Book Art</strong> to add the books&rsquo;
    maps, or pick a destination back on the walkthrough&rsquo;s own list.
  </p>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="stonetop-travel-map-foot">
    {{!-- What a shift-click on the map lays, said under the picture exactly as the route step says
          it. Ahead of the readout, since it is about the picture and the readout is about the
          answer. `sync` re-renders both halves of this foot together. --}}
    {{> "stonetop.expedition-journey-drawhint" journey=journey}}
    {{> "stonetop.expedition-journey-route" journey=journey}}
  </div>
</div>
